  "project": {
    "name": "Engram",
    "description": "",
    "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T13:30:17Z"
  },
  "memory": [
    {
      "key": "single-writer",
      "category": "invariant",
      "status": "active",
      "pinned": true,
      "content": [
        "Every mutation of a `.engram` file goes through `engram_core::ops::Op` executed inside `Store::transact`.",
        "",
        "- The macOS app reaches it via the C ABI (`engram_apply`).",
        "- Agents reach it via `engram-mcp` tools.",
        "- Nothing else writes the file."
      ],
      "files": [
        "rust-core/crates/engram-core/src/ops.rs",
        "rust-core/crates/engram-core/src/store.rs"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "atomic-writes",
      "category": "invariant",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "Writes take an exclusive `flock` on the sidecar `.<name>.engram.lock`, re-read from disk, validate, then replace the file with temp + fsync + rename. Concurrent writers must never lose updates.",
      "files": [
        "rust-core/crates/engram-core/src/store.rs"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "tech-stack",
      "category": "tech_stack",
      "status": "active",
      "content": [
        "- **Core:** Rust 2021, serde_json, tiktoken-rs (o200k_base), tokio for the stdio server",
        "- **macOS app:** SwiftUI, Swift 5.9 language mode, macOS 14 and later",
        "- **Windows and Linux app:** eframe/egui 0.37 with the glow backend, rfd for native file dialogs",
        "- **Bridge:** static `libengram_core.a` + cbindgen header, imported as the `CEngramCore` module"
      ],
      "files": [
        "rust-core/Cargo.toml",
        "EngramApp/Package.swift",
        "rust-core/crates/engram-desktop/Cargo.toml"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T13:30:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "git-friendly-format",
      "category": "rule",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "The `.engram` format is pretty-printed JSON with two-space indent and a trailing newline. Multi-line Markdown is stored as an array of lines so diffs stay line-level. Never reorder arrays on save.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "ffi-envelope",
      "category": "convention",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "FFI calls return a JSON envelope `{ok, data | error{code,message}}`. Strings returned by Rust are freed with `engram_string_free`. Panics are caught at the boundary.",
      "files": [
        "rust-core/crates/engram-core/src/ffi.rs",
        "EngramApp/Sources/Engram/Core/EngramEngine.swift"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "ui-state",
      "category": "convention",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "SwiftUI state lives in `WorkspaceModel` (one per window, `@Observable`). Views never decode files themselves; they read the cached snapshot and send `EngramOp`s.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "build-tooling",
      "category": "note",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "Build with `./build.sh` (universal arm64 + x86_64) or `./build.sh --native --debug` for local iteration; add `--test` to run the Rust and Swift suites. The script assembles `build/Engram.app` and embeds engram-mcp next to the app executable.",
      "files": [
        "build.sh"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T12:50:29Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenizer-old",
      "category": "tech_stack",
      "status": "superseded",
      "content": "Token counts use cl100k_base.",
      "superseded_by": "tokenizer",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenizer",
      "category": "tech_stack",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "Token counts use o200k_base via tiktoken-rs. Counts are deterministic approximations for non-OpenAI models.",
      "files": [
        "rust-core/crates/engram-core/src/tokens.rs"
      ],
      "supersedes": "tokenizer-old",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T08:15:17Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "live-reload-check",
      "category": "note",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "The app live-reloads when engram-mcp writes the open file: the macOS app re-arms a file watcher after each atomic rename, the Windows and Linux app polls the file fingerprint. Both refresh only when the bytes on disk differ from their own snapshot.",
      "files": [
        "EngramApp/Sources/Engram/Core/FileWatcher.swift",
        "rust-core/crates/engram-desktop/src/workspace.rs"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T12:50:12Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T13:21:47Z"
    },
    {
      "key": "localization",
      "category": "convention",
      "status": "active",
      "content": "Every user-facing string is localizable. English is the source language: `String(localized:)` in Swift, `tr()` and `trf()` in the Rust desktop app.",
      "files": [
        "rust-core/crates/engram-desktop/src/i18n.rs"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T13:30:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T13:30:17Z"
    }
  ],
